<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">PRRI rebellion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1958">1958</a>–<a href="/years/1961">1961</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Revolutionary Government of the Republic of Indonesia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The PRRI rebellion was a regional revolt against the central government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, launched when dissident army officers and politicians proclaimed the Revolutionary Government of the Republic of Indonesia in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-sumatra">West Sumatra</a> in February 1958. Opposed to the growing power of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukarno">Sukarno</a> and the communists, and to Javanese domination, the rebels joined forces with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/permesta">Permesta</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a>. Government troops took their towns within months, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> remnants surrendered under an amnesty in 1961.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prri-rebellion.jpg" alt="PRRI rebellion" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BorysMapping · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PRRI_campaign.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the 1950s it suppressed regional rebellions, including the Darul Islam movement, which sought an Islamic state, and the <b>PRRI</b> and Permesta revolts in Sumatra and Sulawesi in 1958.</blockquote><a href="/empire/indonesia">Indonesia · Military</a></li></ul></section>
